   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the elder law, in relation to congregate services initiative for the elderly",
    "basePrintNo": "S8098",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8098-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §217, Eld L",
    "lawSection": "Elder Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S8098\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the elder law, in relation to congregate services\ninitiative for the elderly\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to make financial literacy education and\nelder abuse education and outreach more widely available to seniors\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill would add financial literacy education and elder abuse\neducation and outreach to the list of services authorized to be\nprovided through the congregate services initiative.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nNew\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nFinancial literacy and elder abuse education and outreach are\nimportant tools that can assist in preventing seniors from being\nvictimized. Predators create deceitful strategies and highly developed\nfinancial scams to lure seniors into traps that strip them from their\nbelongings. Providing senior citizens with information regarding money\nmanagement, applying for benefits, and predatory schemes will raise\ntheir awareness and better prepare them in their decision making.\nBroader education regarding elder abuse and outreach will help aid\nseniors to recognize when they or someone they know could be at risk\nfor or caught in an abusive situation and provide resources they may\naccess for help.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
